Commit message:
inline chunks using `import.meta.hot` in dev mode (#11339)

In dev mode (`experimental.devMode`), `experimentalInlineCommonChunks` never inlines a common chunk whose modules use `import.meta.hot`; the chunk always stays a separate file. Vite's production build replaces `import.meta.hot` with `undefined` and inlines the same chunk, so dev and production split the app differently. This PR inlines these chunks in dev mode too.

```js
// self_accept.js, imported by entries a.js and b.js
export const value = 'self-v0';

import.meta.hot.accept((mod) => {
  globalThis.selfAccepted = mod.value;
});
```

