use module types for the module handler

@cloudflare/workers-types 5.20261025 made the global ExecutionContext incompatible with the module one (mapVirtualHost takes a Fetcher).

Commit message:
the ORM and SQL builder read from MySQL, with every value sent as a prepared-statement parameter (#30863)

## At a glance

The MySQL example app now reads through the ORM, imports only
`@prisma/orm-mysql`, and runs against MySQL 8.4 in CI:

```ts
import mysql from '@prisma/orm-mysql/runtime';
import { contractFromJson } from '@prisma/orm-mysql/static';

const db = mysql({ contract: contractFromJson<Contract>(contractJson), url });

// A user with their posts, newest title first
await db.orm.User.include('posts', (posts) => posts.orderBy((p) => p.title.desc())).first({ id: 1 });
